<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
    <!--
        Gives AI-controlled magiers their Self- and Location-targeted psycasts.

        Why the constant tree: VEF only offers abilities to the AI via a Pawn.TryGetAttackVerb
        postfix, which can only pick abilities whose verb can hit the current enemy pawn. Flash,
        Repel, EMP burst and quick draw all target self or a location, so no raider could ever
        use them. HumanlikeConstant is evaluated regardless of the pawn's current job, which is
        what lets the node interrupt a shooting job to blind someone.

        Cost: this node is evaluated for every humanlike on the map. JobGiver_TaktikmagierCombat
        rejects non-AI pawns, unspawned/downed pawns and pawns with no enemy target before doing
        any real work, and only re-evaluates every 30 ticks.

        If this patch ever fails (a future version renaming the tree), RimWorld logs a patch
        error and the mod still loads - AI magiers simply fall back to shooting.
    -->
    <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <!--
            Appended, not prepended, on purpose: the vanilla constant nodes ahead of it handle
            things that must win over casting - escaping fire, dropping a burning weapon,
            reacting to being drafted. A magier who is on fire should run, not cast Flash.
        -->
        <xpath>Defs/ThinkTreeDef[defName="HumanlikeConstant"]/thinkRoot/subNodes</xpath>
        <value>
            <li Class="Militarmagier.JobGiver_TaktikmagierCombat" />
        </value>
    </Operation>
</Patch>
